Adreno-Defibrillator.wikitext:
{{Infobox Armor Passive
|title={{PAGENAME}}
|image={{PAGENAME}} Armor Passive Icon.svg
|description=Provides one-time, short-lived resuscitation upon death, given that the [[Helldiver's]] body is still intact.<br>Increases [[stim]] effect duration by '''<span style=color:var(--wiki-custom-emphasis-color)>2.0s</span>'''.<br>Provides '''<span style=color:var(--wiki-custom-emphasis-color)>50%</span>''' resistance to [[Damage#Damage Types|arc damage]].
|order=19
}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[armor passive]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''.

==Description==
{{Armor Passive Info Panel|{{PAGENAME}}}}


==Functionality==
Upon dying, unless gibbed, the player will ragdoll and health is immediately restored to full. While not under the effects of a stim, vision will turn black and white and audio will be muffled. Revived players suffer a permanent bleed penalty, where their stamina will always be fully depleted and their health constantly drains. Health drains at a rate of approximately 20% per second, and the player can still take damage from enemies as normal. This last stand state ends when the player's health is fully depleted, whether from the health drain or from enemy attacks.

==Tactical Information==
* This armor passive grants players the opportunity to perform a final stand after their health reaches zero.
* In this last stand, you are intended to do as much damage as possible before you fully die, such as with a [[B-100 Portable Hellbomb]], or an [[Eagle 500kg Bomb]] thrown at your feet.<ref>{{cite Discord|url=https://discord.com/channels/1102970375731691612/1204540553971372072/1392859080590233702|channel=the-armory|message=The point of the new armor is to let go with a bang, not give you a second chance in life. Activate a hellbomb backpack, call in a 500kg on yourself, take the biggest mf with you.|author=Alexus Kravchenko|date=2025-07-10}}</ref>
* Using a [[Stim]] can prolong the duration of the last stand, however the health drain is permanent and can never be stopped.
* Boarding the [[Pelican]] in a last stand state will count as a successful [[extraction]], as your Helldiver will still [[Victory Pose|pose victoriously]] upon returning to the [[Destroyer]] instead of standing to the side.
* Each stim used by the wearer, whether on themselves or on a teammate, lasts 2.0 seconds longer.
** The increased stim duration can allow the patient to endure damage for longer periods of time before the effects expire. Principally, this means that players under the effects of the stim have a bigger window during which they will emerge from the stim's effects with full health.
** The stim will also increase the duration of the last stand state, allowing the player to continue dealing damage over a longer period of time.
* The armor also provides 50% resistance to electrical attacks from certain types of [[Illuminate]]s or friendly fire arcs from other Helldivers.

