|image={{PAGENAME}} Armor Passive Icon.svg
|description=Wearer makes '''<span style=color:var(--wiki-custom-emphasis-color)>50%</span>''' less noise when moving.<br>Increases [[Minor Places of Interest|point-of-interest]] identification range by '''<span style=color:var(--wiki-custom-emphasis-color)>30%</span>'''.<br>Provides immunity to leg injuries.
|order=20
}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[armor passive]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''.

== Description ==
{{Armor Passive Info Panel|{{PAGENAME}}}}

== Explanation ==
<span style=color:var(--wiki-heading-color)>'''1.'''</span>
Reduces any movement noise: walking, crouching, crawling, slipping from terrain, etc. by 50%. In most situations, enemies will be unable to hear [[Helldiver]]s.
It also reduces noise made by [[LIFT-850 Jump Pack|Jump Pack]] and [[LIFT-860 Hover Pack|Hover Pack]] on lifting and landing stages.<ref>[https://youtu.be/MXOS5G94tcU Jump Pack and Hover Pack Noise Reduction]</ref>

<br><span style=color:var(--wiki-heading-color)>'''2.'''</span>
Objective-based [[Minor Places of Interest]] are called out by Helldivers from 30% further away. This increases the 54-56m mPOI detection range to 70-72m, approximately 14-16m further from normal. This also affects the <code>?</code> that appears on the map whenever a mPOI is nearby.

'''(a)''' This only applies to objective-based [[Minor Places of Interest]], or those that count towards [[Secondary Objectives]].

'''(b)''' Identification range for Loot-Only based mPOIs are not affected (e.g. mPOIs that hold no tactical value, such as those found during Level 1 [[Difficulty]] missions for farming [[Super Credits]]). Identification range for Loot-Only mPOIs remains unchanged at 54-56m.

<br><span style=color:var(--wiki-heading-color)>'''3.'''</span>
A Helldiver's legs will not break when taking damage. This includes friendly fire and fall damage, as well as instantaneous leg-injuries from rapid double-use of the [[Warp Pack]].

