Supplemental Adrenaline.wikitext:
{{Infobox Armor Passive
|title={{PAGENAME}}
|image={{PAGENAME}} Armor Passive Icon.svg
|description=When the wearer takes damage, they regain some stamina.<br>Provides a '''<span style=color:var(--wiki-custom-emphasis-color)>higher [[Damage#Armor Damage Modifiers|armor rating]]</span>'''.
|order=23
}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[armor passive]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''.

== Description ==
{{Armor Passive Info Panel|{{PAGENAME}}}}

== Explanation ==
{{Incomplete section|the amount of stamina regained when taking damage}}
Increases the wearer's armor rating by 25 points without reducing speed or stamina regeneration.

Normally, torso hits reduce both health and stamina, while hits to other body sections reduce health without depleting stamina.

Supplemental Adrenaline restores stamina when the wearer takes damage. The observed refund differs between enemies: Terminid Scavenger and Warrior hits consistently restore approximately a full stamina bar, whereas Voteless attacks and tested Automaton attacks generally appear to follow damage-based scaling—approximately two points of stamina restored per point of maximum health lost, up to a full bar. Overseer plasma projectiles also showed this scaling.

Torso hits still inflict stamina damage, which can offset the refund in certain situations like Cyborg shotgun attacks. Limb injuries reduce the observed refund. Chest hemorrhage triggers a small stamina refund with each bleed tick, while a broken leg prevents sprinting even when stamina is restored.{{Msgbox|mini=1|title=Note|type=notice|text=If the total [[body armor]] rating exceeds 100, the [[Helldiver]] takes less [[damage]] from headshots as well.}}

